text:
mina: quick callout from the console review: the compact action group (icon+label buttons) in the header looks visually tight at 340px. feels crowded next to the search pill. screenshot: https://img.redwood.example/console/compact-action-group.png
owen: yep that's the inline gap token. today it's `--space-compact-inline: 6px`. for icon+label combos i think 10px works much better for rhythm and tap targets.
chi: instead of changing that global token, can we add a scoped token like `--space-inline-actions: 10px` and only apply it to header/row action groups? low risk.
tara: agree on a scoped token. also noticed the ghost secondary button in the toolbar has an invisible hit area on touch because visual size is 36px. we should ensure a 44px minimum hit area via padding or invisible overlay. propose `--touch-target-min: 44px`.
mina: good point. small CSS snippets:```css
:root { --space-inline-actions: 10px; --touch-target-min: 44px; }
.header .action + .action { margin-left: var(--space-inline-actions); }
.action--icon { padding: calc((var(--touch-target-min) - 32px) / 2); }
```
owen: accessibility nit: when header CTA opens the deploy drawer, focus doesn't reliably move into the drawer on Safari VoiceOver. modal/drawer component should set `role="dialog"` + `aria-modal="true"` and focus the primary element on open.
chi: sample JS:```js
onOpen(drawer) {
  drawer.setAttribute('role','dialog');
  drawer.setAttribute('aria-modal','true');
  const auto = drawer.querySelector('[data-autofocus]') || drawer.querySelector('button, input, a');
  setTimeout(() => auto && auto.focus(), 0);
}
```
tara: toasts: we currently show transient error toasts for deploy failures with a 2s timeout. keyboard & screen reader users flag this as too short. suggest error toasts be actionable and persistent for 6s or until dismissed when they include a Retry. also use `role="alert"` for errors and `aria-live="polite"` for info/success. make actionable toasts tabindex=0 so keyboard users can reach Retry.
mina: agree. proposed toast semantics: error -> role=alert, tabindex=0, duration=6000 (or persistent if contains action). success -> aria-live=polite, duration=2500. example markup:```html
<div class="toast toast--error" role="alert" tabindex="0" data-duration="6000">
  Deploy failed. <button aria-label="Retry deploy">Retry</button>
</div>
```
owen: also spotted z-index shuffling: toasts sometimes render above drawers/modals and block their close buttons. we should adopt tokenized layers like `--z-drawer: 800`, `--z-toast: 700` and ensure drawers are above toasts.
chi: good call. i'll add tokens/layers.json with a simple stacking map and update components to consume it.
tara: copy nit: header CTA says "Kick off" while drawer primary uses "Start deploy". pick one. i vote for "Start deploy" (clearer). i'll update the copy tokens file.
mina: next steps: chi adds `--space-inline-actions` + `--touch-target-min` tokens and a Storybook story at 340px for the header; chi also adds layer tokens. owen will patch drawer focus handling. tara will update copy tokens to "Start deploy" and add an a11y story for actionable error toasts. we'll snapshot the new header story in CI and run axe on new stories.
a11y-bot: queued a11y smoke for new stories; reminder: actionable toasts must be keyboard dismissible and have clear aria-labels on buttons.
mina: thanks all — i'll open a tracking PR with the token/story bits, then follow-ups for runtime changes. closing loop here. :white_check_mark:
